# --- Rust build output ---
/target/
**/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Cargo.lock IS committed deliberately: this repo produces a binary, not a
# library, so a pinned dependency graph is what makes builds reproducible.

# --- .NET build output (the window, in /ui-wpf) ---
**/bin/
**/obj/

# --- Release output, reproducible from tools/build-release.ps1 ---
/dist/
*.exe
*.dll
*.msi

# --- Lanes runtime state ---
# This lives in %LOCALAPPDATA%\Lanes\ (or beside a portable copy) and never
# belongs in the repository. Listed anyway as belt and braces: config.json
# holds the local API's shared token, and snapshots and logs describe a
# machine and the applications on it.
config.json
/port
port.txt
portable.txt
test-apps.txt
/Lanes/
snapshots/
logs/
*.log

# --- Editors and tooling ---
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.claude/

# --- Windows ---
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
